# FABLE-SONNET-NODE-ROOT-20260923-121: E itself has no lexical parent (the
# unit IS E's own occurrence) -- node\x anywhere in E's own top-level body
# must refuse, never resolve to E itself or silently read/write nothing.
# l2_path_root leaves "node" unresolved here, so l2_is_path_head is false
# and the existing multi-segment-head guard in l2_check_body refuses with
# "unknown field path root" (measured; not the author's own informal
# "unresolved name" for his flawed Q9 example, which was never about this
# exact diagnostic string -- the outcome, refusal, is what Q9 requires).
int: x 1
node\x: 9
return: 0
